CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F319A1786105098
OL,3,CNearly 10,000 people referred to UK
OL,4,Canti-terror programme in decade high
OL,6,FThe figures, published on Thursday,
OL,7,Falso show that 2,103 referrals (20%)
OL,8,Fwere linked to concerns about extreme
OL,9,Fright-wing ideology, up from 1,480 in
OL,10,Fthe past 12 months.
OL,12,FMeanwhile, referrals relating to
OL,13,FIslamist extremism fell slightly to
OL,14,F860 (8%), down from 945.
OL,16,FThere were also 818 referrals (8%)
OL,17,Finvolving a fascination with extreme
OL,18,Fviolence or mass casualty attacks, 95
OL,19,F(1%) related to incel (involuntarily
OL,20,Fcelibate) extremism, and 32 (0.3%)
OL,21,Frelated to left-wing extremism.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
