OL,3,CNearly 10,000 people referred to UK
OL,4,Canti-terror programme in decade high
OL,6,FThe figures also show that more than a
OL,7,Fthird (36%) of people referred to
OL,8,FPrevent in the year to September had
OL,9,Fat least one recorded neurodiversity
OL,10,For mental health condition.
OL,12,FAutism was the most commonly recorded
OL,13,Fneurodiversity condition, affecting
OL,14,F1,833 people (18%), followed by a
OL,15,Flearning disorder, recorded in 279
OL,16,Fcases (3%).
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/10
